id: pm-vcs-v4z8
title: Refresh verified stat cache after materialization without trusting concurrent bytes
description: "Cubic review exposed a tension in the initial materialization cache: recording a post-write stat can pair the expected object id with bytes concurrently replaced by another process, while omitting metadata makes status re-read restored or switched files until a later stage. Design a safe cache warm-up that verifies content and updates metadata only after the timestamp window, without turning a read-only status into a racy index overwrite."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: concurrency,performance,review-followup,stat-cache
created_at: "2026-08-01T04:50:06.115Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-01T04:50:06.115Z"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "After restore or switch, an aged unchanged file reaches metadata-only status without explicit add; a concurrent write at every materialization and refresh boundary is detected; index updates use compare-and-swap or locking so status cannot overwrite a concurrent stage; installed-CLI strace acceptance proves content reads stop; full coverage remains 100/100/100"
parent: pm-vcs-tr2a
severity: medium
expected_result: Materialized files safely warm the stat cache and later status calls avoid content reads.
actual_result: Correctness-first materialization currently omits stat metadata because an unverified post-write stat can hide a concurrent edit.
component: engine/worktree
